#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:128
msgid ""
"apt-get update fetches the newest lists of updates from your software "
"sources. Nothing is installed."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:131
msgid "--update first fetches the newest lists of updates."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:133
msgid "upgrade installs the updates that are waiting."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:134
msgid ""
"--with-new-pkgs may also install new packages an update needs; it never "
"removes any."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:138
msgid ""
"install --reinstall installs these packages again, which puts their own "
"files back."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:142
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:151
msgid "-y answers yes on your behalf, so it does not stop to ask."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:143
msgid ""
"The two --force-conf options: where you have changed a settings file and the "
"package brings a new one, your version is kept."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:145
msgid "Packages that are not signed are never installed: apt stops instead."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:148
msgid ""
"add-apt-repository sets the PPA up again for the release this computer runs, "
"with its signing key from Launchpad, and then fetches the lists of updates."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:152
msgid ""
"Afterwards, the program checks that the PPA could be read for this release: "
"add-apt-repository does not say so itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:156
msgid "enable --now switches the jobs on now, and at every start."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:157
msgid ""
"apt-daily.timer looks for updates every day; apt-daily-upgrade.timer "
"installs them, as set up."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:160
msgid ""
"sudo runs it with administrator rights. From this page, the switch beside "
"the title asks for the password."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:163
msgid ""
"It cannot be undone from here: what it changes is up to the tool and the "
"packages, and not all of it can be known beforehand."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:196
msgid ""
"The PPA was set up, but could not be read for this release, so it most "
"likely has no packages for it yet. It now gives the same error every time "
"updates are looked for, so switch it off again: in Software & Updates, under "
"Other Software, take the tick off its line for this release."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:227
msgid "Switch On"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:228
msgid ""
"Writes the program's own file /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/52gaudit-automatic-"
"updates: this computer then looks for updates every day and installs them as "
"unattended-upgrades is set up (on Debian and Ubuntu: security updates). It "
"can be removed again here."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:234
msgid "Remove the Program's Setting"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:235
msgid ""
"Removes the program's own file /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/52gaudit-automatic-"
"updates, if it is still as the program wrote it. Settings made elsewhere are "
"not touched."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:243
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:250
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:266
msgid "Install Updates Automatically"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:244
msgid "The program has set this computer up to install updates by itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:245
msgid ""
"It is the program's own setting, and it can be taken away again here. Then "
"the computer's other settings decide."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:251
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:267
msgid ""
"Updates are not installed by themselves on this computer, so it is only as "
"up to date as the last time someone installed them."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:253
msgid ""
"The program can switch it on with a setting of its own: security updates are "
"then installed by themselves. You are asked to confirm first, and it can be "
"taken away again here."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:256
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:273
msgid ""
"If it is off on purpose, for example because changes must be planned, keep "
"it off and install the updates regularly yourself."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: %s is a list of programs, e.g. "update-manager, synaptic".
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:261
#, c-format
msgid ""
"Switch it on in your update program (%s): choose to install security updates "
"automatically. Other updates can still wait for you."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:270
msgid ""
"In your system's settings for software updates, choose to install security "
"updates automatically. Other updates can still wait for you."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: the newest version, the one installed, who makes it (three
#. * times), then the address of their download page.
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:370
#, c-format
msgid ""
"Version %s is out; this computer has %s. %s does not sign its package, so "
"the program cannot check that %s made it, and does not install it. Download "
"it from %s's own page: %s"
msgstr ""

#. Translators: the newest version, the one installed, then who makes it.
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:379
#, c-format
msgid ""
"Version %s is out; this computer has %s. The program can download it from "
"%s, check that %s signed it, and install it."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:388
#, c-format
msgid "This computer has the newest version, %s."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:392
msgid ""
"It could not be found out. The page may not answer, or this computer may "
"have no connection."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:475
msgid "Looking for the newest version…"
msgstr ""

#. Translators: a program's name, then its version.
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:488
#, c-format
msgid "Installed: %s now has version %s."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:490
msgid ""
"Installing stopped with an error. Look for updates and try again, or install "
"it from the maker's page."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:493
msgid "The download could not be read, so nothing was installed."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:495
msgid ""
"The download is larger than the program accepts, so nothing was installed."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:497
msgid ""
"The package is not signed, so who made it cannot be checked. It was not "
"installed."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: %s is who makes the program, twice.
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:502
#, c-format
msgid ""
"The package is signed with a key the program does not know for %s, so it was "
"not installed. If %s has changed its key, a newer version of the program "
"will know it; until then, install it from the maker's page yourself."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:506
msgid "The signature does not match the package. It was not installed."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:508
msgid ""
"The signature rests on MD5 alone, which says nothing about who made the "
"package. It was not installed."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:511
msgid ""
"The package's contents do not match its signature. It was not installed."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:514
msgid ""
"The download is not the package and version expected. It was not installed."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:517
msgid ""
"The download is not newer than the version installed. It was not installed."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:520
msgid ""
"The checked package is gone, for one when the administrator rights ended in "
"between. Nothing was installed."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:522
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:535
msgid "It could not be checked or installed."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:529
msgid "Cancelled, so nothing was installed."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:553
msgid ""
"Installing… It needs administrator rights: use the switch beside the title "
"if asked."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:558
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:626
msgid "It is already under way."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: who makes it, then a hash method's name, e.g. SHA1.
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:581
#, c-format
msgid ""
"The package is signed by %s with the key the program knows for it, and every "
"part of it matches the signature. But the signature uses %s, an older method "
"that apt no longer accepts for software sources. Install it anyway, or go "
"back."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:585
msgid "Checked."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:621
msgid ""
"Downloaded. Checking the signature… It needs administrator rights: use the "
"switch beside the title if asked."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:634
msgid "It could not be downloaded, so nothing was installed."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:646
msgid "Downloading…"
msgstr ""

#. Translators: %s is a program's name, e.g. "Zoom".
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:673
#, c-format
msgid "Update %s Yourself"
msgstr ""

#. Translators: a program's name, its version, then who makes it.
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:676
#, c-format
msgid ""
"%s (version %s) is installed from a package %s offers only as a download, "
"without a software source. So the system never updates it, not even with "
"security fixes."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: %s is who makes the program.
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:681
#, c-format
msgid ""
"Best is a software source: then the system updates it with everything else. "
"Look for one from %s itself, or from someone you trust; the key of a source "
"decides what is installed on this computer, so the choice is yours."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: who makes it, then the address of their download page.
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:686
#, c-format
msgid "Download new versions from %s's own page and install them: %s"
msgstr ""

#. Translators: a Flatpak app id, then who makes the program.
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:692
#, c-format
msgid ""
"Or use it as a Flatpak instead (%s on Flathub), which gets updates. Flathub "
"marks it “Verified”: it is published by %s, or by someone %s has authorized."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: a Flatpak app id, then who makes the program.
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:697
#, c-format
msgid ""
"Or use it as a Flatpak instead (%s on Flathub), which gets updates. Flathub "
"marks it “Unverified”: someone other than %s publishes it, so you trust them "
"as well."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: a Flatpak app id, then who makes the program.
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:702
#, c-format
msgid ""
"Or use it as a Flatpak instead (%s on Flathub), which gets updates. On its "
"page on Flathub, the mark “Verified” (a blue badge) means it is published by "
"%s, or by someone %s has authorized; where the page says “Unverified”, or "
"has no mark, someone else publishes it."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: a snap's name, then who makes the program.
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:710
#, c-format
msgid ""
"Or use it as a snap instead (%s in the Snap Store), which gets updates. It "
"is published by %s itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:722
msgid ""
"Looking for the newest version and installing it here is a fallback for a "
"package without a source: you chose this package, and there may be a good "
"reason for it."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:725
msgid ""
"Looking for the newest version here is a fallback for a package without a "
"source: you chose this package, and there may be a good reason for it."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:740
msgid "Check for a New Version"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:742
msgid ""
"Asks the maker's page which version is the newest. Nothing is downloaded or "
"installed."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:746
msgid "Install"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:748
msgid "Downloads the newer version, checks its signature and installs it"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:754
msgid "Install Anyway"
msgstr ""

#. Translators: %s is a product, e.g. "CUDA".
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:809
#, c-format
msgid "%s From a Local Copy"
msgstr ""

#. Translators: a product, its version, who makes it, the release the copy
#. * was made for (e.g. "Ubuntu 26.04"), then a sentence about the packages.
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:813
#, c-format
msgid ""
"%s %s was installed from a local copy of %s's software source, made for %s. "
"%s"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:815
msgid ""
"The copy never changes, so the package from it never gets updates, not even "
"security fixes."
msgid_plural ""
"The copy never changes, so the packages from it never get updates, not even "
"security fixes."
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#. Translators: the release the copy was made for, then the one running.
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:821
#, c-format
msgid ""
"The copy was made for %s, not for %s, which this computer runs. The program "
"does not recommend using a source made for another release: it was made and "
"tested for that release, against the libraries it has."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: a version (13.3), then a package name (cuda-toolkit-13-3).
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:834
#, c-format
msgid ""
" To stay on version %s, install the package %s: it keeps that version, and "
"still gets its fixes."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: who makes it, the release running, who makes it, the release
#. * running, the download page, the product, then the sentence about one version.
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:839
#, c-format
msgid ""
"%s has a software source for this release (%s). Set it up from %s's download "
"page, choosing the network installer for %s: %s\n"
"\n"
"The system then updates %s with everything else.%s"
msgstr ""

#. Translators: who makes it, the release running, who makes it, its download page.
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:846
#, c-format
msgid ""
"%s has no software source for this release (%s) yet. Look on %s's download "
"page now and then: %s"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:858
msgid ""
"This is a recommendation: staying on a version can be deliberate, such as "
"for a project that needs it. The program downloads and installs nothing for "
"it."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: %s is a release, e.g. "Ubuntu 26.04".
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:868
#, c-format
msgid "Show the Source for %s"
msgstr ""

#. Translators: who makes it, the release before, who makes it, the release before.
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:873
#, c-format
msgid ""
"%s has a source for %s, the release before. Using a source made for an "
"earlier release is not something the program recommends: it was made and "
"tested for that release, against the libraries it has. If you choose it "
"anyway, set it up from %s's download page, choosing %s."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:949
msgid ""
"Files installed by packages were changed or are gone. It may be harmless, "
"such as a program changing its own file, but nothing should change installed "
"files."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:953
msgid ""
"Not every package is in the command: only those listed in the report, with "
"plain names. Check again afterwards to see what is left."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:955
msgid "Afterwards, it is checked again: the files should then match."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:960
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:964
msgid "Put the Package Files Back"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:961
msgid ""
"If you did not change them yourself, reinstall the packages: it puts their "
"own files back, and keeps your settings in /etc."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:965
msgid ""
"If you did not change them yourself, reinstall the packages with your "
"package manager."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:991
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1001
msgid "Look for Updates"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:992
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1002
msgid ""
"This computer never looks for updates, so it never finds security updates "
"either."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:993
msgid ""
"In your system's settings for software updates, choose to look for updates "
"every day. Until then, you can look once yourself."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:996
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1006
msgid "Looking once is not enough: updates come out all the time."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1003
msgid ""
"In your system's settings for software updates, choose to look for updates "
"every day. Until then, you can look once yourself with this command in a "
"terminal."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1016
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1027
msgid "Switch On the Daily Jobs"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1017
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1028
msgid ""
"The jobs that look for and install updates every day are switched off, so "
"the settings for updates have no effect."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1019
msgid "Switch them on again:"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1021
msgid "Afterwards, it is checked again: the jobs should then be listed as on."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1030
msgid "Run this command in a terminal to switch them on again."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1032
msgid "Afterwards, check again: the jobs should then be listed as on."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: %s is one or more sources, e.g. "ppa:cappelikan/ppa".
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1038
#, c-format
msgid ""
"These software sources were switched off when the release was upgraded: %s. "
"Nothing from them gets updates while they are off."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1040
msgid ""
"The upgrade switches off sources it does not know, since they may not have "
"packages for the new release yet; switching one on then gives an error the "
"next time updates are looked for."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1065
msgid ""
"Check the PPA's page on Launchpad first for packages for this release. If it "
"has them, set it up again here. Other sources are switched on in your "
"system's settings for software sources."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1069
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1082
msgid "Software Sources Switched Off"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1070
msgid ""
"Only the PPA's own page can tell whether it is ready: on Launchpad, it must "
"list packages for exactly this release. Packages for older releases are not "
"enough, and neither is this release in the list without packages, so look "
"there before you run the command."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1078
msgid ""
"Check the source's page first (for a PPA, its page on Launchpad) for "
"packages for this release. If it has them, switch it on in your system's "
"settings for software sources."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1083
msgid ""
"The program does not switch them on: only the source's own page can tell "
"whether it is ready for this release."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: %s is one or more host names, e.g. "prerelease.keybase.io".
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1091
#, c-format
msgid ""
"The software source %s is set up, but its lists of packages have never been "
"fetched, so nothing from it gets updates."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1093
msgid ""
"Look for updates: that fetches the lists from every source. If it still "
"cannot be read, the command shows why, often a signing key that is missing "
"or has expired, or a source that no longer exists."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1096
msgid ""
"It often happens after an upgrade of the release, or when a source is added "
"without looking for updates since."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1099
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1101
msgid "Read the Software Source"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1108
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1117
msgid "Look for Updates Now"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1109
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1118
msgid ""
"This computer has not looked for updates for a long time, so it does not "
"know about updates published since."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1111
msgid ""
"Look for them now. If it keeps happening, check that the computer looks for "
"updates by itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1121
msgid ""
"Run this command in a terminal. If it keeps happening, check that the "
"computer looks for updates by itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1123
msgid ""
"Install the updates with the command below; it looks for new ones first."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1140
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1154
msgid "Install the Updates"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1142
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1156
msgid ""
"Security updates are waiting. Until they are installed, the problems they "
"fix stay open on this computer."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1144
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1158
msgid "Updates are waiting, and some of them may be security updates."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1145
msgid "Install them with your system's software updater, or here:"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1147
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1162
msgid "Installing updates automatically keeps this from building up again."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1159
msgid ""
"Install them with your system's software updater, or run this command in a "
"terminal."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: %s is a host name, e.g. no.archive.ubuntu.com.
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1168
#, c-format
msgid ""
"Security updates come from %s, a mirror. A mirror may lag behind, and "
"security updates should not wait."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1171
msgid "Get Security Updates from the Source"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:1172
